<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> In addition to the SCP and description an incident report with video log and an interview with someone present during the incident</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> The SCP is a bunch of melon plants that compel people to eat them through a cognitohazard. Once they've been eaten a similar effect is placed on the head of the person who ate the melon, where other people will chase you to the ends of the earth in order to eat your brains, nose, eyes and all that good stuff.<br />
Edit: The effect does not transfer to those who ate the infected person, but a new plant wil grow out of their skull after a couple weeks, killing them in the process.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> One of the members of the team that went to retrieve the SCP was pulled in by its effect and then eaten by the rest of their team members. The video log in the incident report and interview will show two perspectives on the horrors that unfolded, with the log showing an objective perspective and the interview a hazy and traumatized perspective.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> It's very much inspired by zombie stories, at least the part where your friends become the monsters you have to fight.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I'm new to writing these articles and don't know every object on the site, so I don't know if this sort of stuff is something that's been done to death</p>

