									</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/westamage" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4472750); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4472750&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606851823" alt="Westamage" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4472750)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/westamage" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4472750); return false;" >Westamage</a></span> <span class="odate time_1606845815 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">01 Dec 2020 18:03</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13891903/idea:intertemporal-boots-stay-with-me-here">Idea: Intertemporal Boots (Stay With Me Here)</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4833786">
									

<p>The SCP is a pair of boots. They would either be made from cloth and have a magical 'Serpent's Hand' sort of feel, or be completely robotic/futuristic. The file would go over the basic mechanics of the boots and testing would include D-Class being thrown throughout various time periods only to have the Foundation return them via some sort of temporal anchor.</p>
<p>Nothing crazy at first, walking forward on the x and z axis causes the user to jump forward in time. Walking backward on the x and z-axis causes them to jump backward in time. The file should get weirder when the D-Class starts moving on the y-axis. This segment would be heavily redacted/classified, but I think the file should imply that the D-Class is visiting other timelines that lay parallel to our own. (It's this part were I would need the most help on brainstorming ideas.)</p>
<p>Just an idea, but it would be a real hoot to write. I'm aiming for more of a Series I/II feel with this article. Nothing world-ending about this SCP, just some anomalous dimension shifting.</p>

							</div>

								
					
